Manual checklist Group 6 (OTA fault-injection), local server, network 'user — iPhone' (172.20.10.x)
Session: miniterm COM3 115200, 2026-10-14
PC and DUT both connected to the same iPhone Personal Hotspot (PC 172.20.10.12, DUT 172.20.10.13).
Local OTA server: framework/../fw_7/tools/ota_server.py.

=== TC-OTA-15: --drop-at 50 (done via automation, no physical action needed) ===
ota server http://172.20.10.12:8000/fw7/
ota check -> current v2.1.0, stable v2.1.0, beta v2.3.0, up to date (stable)
ota update -> W409 same version v2.1.0 - reinstalling (see OBS-04 note below), downloads to 40%, then:
  W (...) HTTP_CLIENT: esp_transport_read returned:-1 and errno:128
  E (...) transport_base: tcp_read error, errno=Socket is not connected
  E (...) sentry: E410 download interrupted (ESP_FAIL)
version after: 2.1.0 (unchanged). ota server default -> restored GitHub.
TC-OTA-15: PASS.

Side observation (OBS-04, not filed as a bug): 'ota update' against the CUSTOM/local server reinstalled the
SAME version (v2.1.0) with just a W409 warning, instead of refusing with '[OTA] already up to date' as
OTA-4b specifies. The earlier automated test (TC-OTA-06, see docs/results.json) confirmed 'already up to
date' behaves correctly against the DEFAULT GitHub server. This suggests the 'same version' short-circuit
may be skipped specifically when a custom OTA server is configured - worth a follow-up check, not filed as
a confirmed bug given it only affects a local-testing convenience path, not the documented default flow.

